# 1. VPC (Virtual Private Cloud)
 VPC ek private virtual network hota hai jo AWS cloud ke andar banta hai.
Jaise company ka apna office hota hai, waise hi AWS me VPC aapka private network hota hai jisme aap EC2, RDS, Load Balancer aur dusre resources rakhte ho.

Simple Example
AWS = City
VPC = Aapka Ghar
EC2 = Ghar ke Rooms
Dusra koi bina permission ke andar nahi aa sakta.

> Kyu use hota hai?
Security provide karta hai.
Network ko control karne ke liye.
Resources ko private rakhne ke liye.
Traffic manage karne ke liye.

> Kaise kaam karta hai?
User browser me amazon.com open karta hai.
Request pehle Load Balancer tak jaati hai.
Load Balancer request ko Web Server (EC2) ko bhejta hai.
Web Server Application Server se data maangta hai.
Application Server Database (RDS) se product ki information leta hai.
Product ki details user ko dikh jaati hain.

> Ek aur Real Example (College)
Maan lo tumhare college ka Attendance Management System AWS par host hai.

VPC
│
├── Public Subnet
│      └── EC2 (Attendance Website)
│
└── Private Subnet
       └── MySQL Database
Student website open karega → Public EC2.
EC2 database se attendance fetch karega.
Database ko koi student directly access nahi kar sakta, kyunki wo Private Subnet me hai.

>> why we need VPC

Q1. What is a VPC?
Answer: A VPC is a private virtual network in AWS where we launch and manage AWS resources securely.

Q2. What is an IP Address?
Answer: An IP address is a unique identifier assigned to every device or resource in a network.

Q3. What is a Subnet?
Answer: A subnet is a smaller network created inside a VPC to organize and isolate AWS resources.


