#  Internet Gateway (IGW)
Kya hai?
Internet Gateway ek gate hai jo VPC ko Internet se connect karta hai.
Agar IGW nahi hoga, to internet se koi connection nahi hoga.
> Real Example
Tumhari company ka office hai.
Office ke bahar ek main gate hai.
-Gate khula → Log andar aur bahar aa sakte hain.
-Gate band → Koi nahi aa sakta.
IGW = Office ka Main Gate

> Kyo Use Hota Hai?
Internet se connect karne ke liye.
Public website chalane ke liye.
Public EC2 ko internet dene ke liye.

> Kab Use Hota Hai?
Jab EC2 ko internet se access karna ho.
Example:
Web Server
Nginx Server
Portfolio Website
WordPress

# NAT Gateway
Kya hai?
NAT Gateway private server ko sirf Internet use karne deta hai, lekin Internet se koi us server tak nahi aa sakta.

Real Example
Company me Accounts Department hai.
Accounts wale bahar ja sakte hain (bank, market), lekin bahar wala aadmi directly Accounts room me nahi aa sakta.

> Kyo Use Hota Hai?
Private EC2 ko:
Software download karna hai.
Windows/Linux update karna hai.
Docker image pull karni hai.
GitHub clone karna hai.

Lekin koi Internet se us server ko access na kare.

> Kab Use Hota Hai?
Private subnet me EC2 ho aur usko internet chahiye.

Example:
App Server
Backend Server
Database Server (normally internet access bhi avoid kiya jata hai)

# Route Table
Kya hai?
Route Table ek Google Maps ki tarah hoti hai.
Ye batati hai:
Data ko kis raste bhejna hai.
Destination          Go Through
0.0.0.0/0        → Internet Gateway
10.0.2.0/24      → Local

> Real Example
Tum GPS me location dalte ho.
Google Maps batata hai kis road se jana hai.
AWS me ye kaam Route Table karti hai.
> Kyo Use Hota Hai?
Network traffic ko direction dene ke liye.
Ye decide karti hai:
Internet jana hai?
Private subnet jana hai?
NAT Gateway jana hai?
Local VPC me rehna hai?
> Kab Use Hota Hai?
Har subnet ke saath Route Table attach hoti hai.

# Security Group (SG)
Kya hai?
Security Group EC2 Instance ka Firewall hai.
Ye decide karta hai:
Kaun andar aa sakta hai aur kaun nahi.

> Real Example
Tumhare ghar ka security guard.
Sirf family ko andar aane deta hai.
Unknown person ko mana kar deta hai.
> Kyo Use Hota Hai?
EC2 ko secure rakhne ke liye.
Example:
SSH allow karna
HTTP allow karna
HTTPS allow karna
> Kab Use Hota Hai?
Jab bhi EC2 launch karte ho.
Har EC2 ke saath ek Security Group attach hota hai.

# Network ACL (NACL)
Kya hai?
NACL Subnet ka Firewall hai.
Security Group EC2 ko protect karta hai.
NACL poore Subnet ko protect karta hai.
> Real Example
Apartment ke gate par security.
Sabko check karega.
Chahe kisi bhi flat me jana ho.
> Kyo Use Hota Hai?
Poore subnet ki security ke liye.
> Kab Use Hota Hai?
Jab subnet level par rules lagane ho.
Example:
Ek pura subnet block karna.
Kisi IP Range ko deny karna.

# Ports
Kya hai?
Port ek door (gate) hota hai.
Har service ka apna door hota hai.
Real Example
Hospital me:
Room 101 → Doctor
Room 102 → Pharmacy
Room 103 → Reception
> Kyo Use Hota Hai?
Computer ko pata chale kis service tak request bhejni hai.



>> Security Group
Security Group is an instance-level firewall that controls inbound and outbound traffic for an EC2 instance.

>> Network ACL
Network ACL is a subnet-level firewall that controls traffic entering and leaving a subnet. It supports both allow and deny rules.

>> Ports
A port is a communication endpoint used by applications. Different services use different port numbers, such as 22 for SSH, 80 for HTTP, and 443 for HTTPS.

