# Route 53 
Route 53 is a highly available and scalable DNS (Domain Name System) web service provided by AWS. 
It translates a domain name (like www.example.com) into an IP address (like 192.168.1.10) so users can access websites and applications.

Example
Domain Name: www.amazon.com
Route 53 finds the corresponding IP address.
Browser connects to that server.
Website opens.

> Key Features
🌐 Domain Registration
🔍 DNS Management
⚖️ Traffic Routing (Latency, Weighted, Geolocation, Failover)
❤️ Health Checks
🔄 High Availability & Automatic Failover

> Use Cases
Hosting website domains
Routing traffic to EC2, ALB, CloudFront, S3
Disaster recovery (Failover)
Load balancing across regions

